,"text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/Notehead-swift.struct/Value-swift.enum":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/notehead-swift.struct\/value-swift.enum","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Value","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The notehead-value type indicates shapes other than the open and closed ovals associated with note durations.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/Notehead-swift.struct\/Value-swift.enum","title":"MXLNote.Notehead.Value","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/Notehead-swift.struct/Value-swift.enum/!=(_:_:)":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"!=(_:_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{